# Overview {#overview}

ImgArchive Studio creates [b].iarc[/b] archive files from sequential image folders.

Instead of storing every image, the system uses [color:accent]AI-powered compression[/color]:

• [color:green]Keyframes[/color] — Full images stored as compressed WebP
• [color:cyan]Interpolated[/color] — NOT stored. Reconstructed on-the-fly using RIFE
• [color:yellow]Residual[/color] — RIFE reconstruction + stored correction patch
• [color:accent]Forced Keyframe[/color] — Stored due to face/body/scene cut risk

This typically achieves [b]70-90% reduction[/b] in disk space.

