# Quick Start Guide {#quick_start}

### Step 1: Select Source Folder
Open the [b]Archive Builder[/b] tab. Click [color:cyan]Browse[/color] to select your image folder.

### Step 2: Scan Folder
Click [color:cyan]Scan[/color]. The app finds all supported images (PNG, JPG, WebP, BMP, TIFF).

### Step 3: Configure Settings
Adjust the build options on the right panel:
• [b]Quality[/b] — WebP compression quality (50-100, default 92)
• [b]GOP Size[/b] — Group of Pictures size (4-48, default 12)
• [b]Similarity Threshold[/b] — How similar frames must be (0.80-0.99)

### Step 4: Analyze Sequence
Click [color:accent]🔍 Analyze Sequence[/color]. The fast 4-phase analyzer runs:

[mono]
Phase 1: Histogram scan      (~1ms/frame, all frames)
Phase 2: Thumbnail SSIM      (~5ms/frame, uncertain only)
Phase 3: AI face/body/motion  (~100ms/frame, risk frames only)
Phase 4: Build compression plan
[/mono]

### Step 5: Review Results
Check the analysis results panel. Review keyframe ratio and estimated savings.

### Step 6: Build Archive
Click [color:green]🔨 Build Archive[/color]. The .iarc file is created.

### Step 7: View & Extract
Switch to [b]Archive Viewer[/b] tab. Open the archive. Browse, decode, and extract frames.

