# Archive Builder {#archive_builder}

## Source & Output

• [b]Source Folder[/b] — Folder containing sequential images
• [b]Output Archive[/b] — Path for the .iarc file (auto-suggested)

## Build Options

### Compression
• [b]Codec[/b] — WebP Lossy (recommended) or JPEG
• [b]Quality[/b] — 50-100. Higher = better quality, larger file
• [b]Chroma[/b] — Subsampling mode (4:2:0 default)

### Sequence Handling
• [b]GOP Size[/b] — Frames between keyframes. Smaller = more keyframes, better quality
• [b]Similarity Threshold[/b] — SSIM threshold. Frames below this become keyframes

### AI Analysis Toggles
• [color:green]Face-Safe Mode[/color] — Detect faces, prevent quality loss on facial regions
• [color:green]Body-Safe Mode[/color] — Detect human bodies, preserve limb transitions
• [color:green]Keep Residuals[/color] — Store correction patches for risky interpolations
• [color:green]Scene Cut Detection[/color] — Detect hard cuts using histogram analysis
• [color:green]Optical Flow (RAFT)[/color] — Use RAFT for motion scoring
• [color:green]Identity Check[/color] — Verify face identity consistency across GOPs
• [color:dim]Archive Downscale[/color] — Store at reduced resolution (optional)
• [color:dim]Depth-Aware[/color] — Use Depth Anything for guided compression (optional)

### Compression Modes
• [b]Max Compression[/b] — Smallest file, more GPU on extract
• [b]Balanced[/b] — Good compression with fast extraction (recommended)
• [b]Fast Access[/b] — Larger file, minimal decode cost

