# Archive Viewer {#archive_viewer}

## Opening an Archive
• Click [color:cyan]📁 Open Archive[/color] in the toolbar
• Or use [b]Ctrl+O[/b]
• Or select from [b]File → Recent Archives[/b]

## Frame List
The left panel shows all frames with:
• [b]Index[/b] — Frame number
• [b]Name[/b] — Original filename
• [b]Type[/b] — K (Keyframe), I (Interpolated), R (Residual), C (Forced), D (Deleted)
• [b]Size[/b] — Stored data size
• [b]Scores[/b] — Similarity, face, and body scores

## Search & Filter
• [b]Search[/b] — Find frames by name or index
• [b]Filter[/b] — Show only specific frame types
• [b]Go to[/b] — Jump to a specific frame index

## Preview
• Click a frame to see its metadata
• Double-click or press [b]Space[/b] to decode and preview
• Use [b]Left/Right arrows[/b] to navigate
• Scroll to zoom, drag to pan, double-click to fit

## Extraction
• [color:yellow]Extract Selected[/color] — Save selected frame(s) to disk
• [color:yellow]Extract Range[/color] — Extract a range of frames by index
• [color:yellow]Extract All[/color] — Extract all frames to a folder
• [color:cyan]Export KFs Only[/color] — Fast export of keyframes only (no GPU needed)

## Frame Management
• [color:red]Delete Selected[/color] — Mark frame(s) as deleted (logical, reversible)
• [color:green]Restore[/color] — Undo deletion
• [color:accent]Compact Archive[/color] — Permanently remove deleted frames
• [color:red]Repair Archive[/color] — Fix corrupted data and broken references

