# Export to Video {#export_video}

Export the archive as a video file with optional audio.

## Requirements
• [b]ffmpeg[/b] must be in your system PATH

## Settings
• [b]Output format[/b] — MP4, WebM, AVI, MKV
• [b]FPS[/b] — 24, 29, 30, or 60 frames per second
• [b]Quality (CRF)[/b] — Lower = better quality (18-28 typical)
• [b]Audio file[/b] — Optional MP3/WAV/AAC/M4A/OGG to mux with video

## How It Works
[mono]
1. Each frame is decoded on-the-fly (GPU for interpolated frames)
2. Raw BGR frames are piped to ffmpeg via stdin
3. ffmpeg encodes to the selected format
4. If audio is selected, it is muxed with -shortest flag
[/mono]

## Access
• Menu: [b]Export → Export to Video...[/b]
• Shortcut: [b]Ctrl+Shift+V[/b]

