# Models & Settings {#models_settings}

## RIFE (Frame Interpolation)
Used for on-the-fly frame reconstruction during extraction.
• [b]Model Directory[/b] — Contains RIFE model files
• GPU/CUDA required for acceptable speed
• FP16 recommended (faster, less VRAM)

## RAFT (Optical Flow)
Used during analysis for motion scoring.
• [b]Variants[/b] — things (recommended), chairs, kitti, sintel, small
• Runs on GPU

## TransNetV2 (Scene Cut Detection)
Detects hard scene cuts in the image sequence.
• Falls back to histogram comparison if model unavailable

## Face Analysis
• [b]InsightFace[/b] — Face detection and landmarks
• [b]BiSeNet (79999_iter.pth)[/b] — Face region parsing
• [b]ArcFace (w600k_r50.onnx)[/b] — Identity consistency checking

## Body Analysis
• [b]YOLO11x-Seg[/b] — Human segmentation
• [b]YOLO11x-Pose[/b] — Body keypoint detection
• [b]DeepLabV3+[/b] — Lightweight human segmentation (fallback)

## Optional Models
• [b]Depth Anything V2[/b] — Depth-guided compression (toggle)
• [b]RealESRGAN / SwinIR[/b] — Post-decode upscaling (toggle)
• [b]GFPGAN[/b] — Face enhancement (toggle, preview/extraction/both)

## Device Settings
• [b]Device[/b] — CUDA (default) or CPU
• [b]Precision[/b] — FP16 (default) or FP32
• [b]Batch Size[/b] — Decode batch size (1 default)

