# Frame Types Explained {#frame_types}

[mono]
Type   Label   Color    Storage            Decode Method
-----  -----   ------   -------            -------------
K      Green   Stored   WebP decode        Direct
I      Blue    None     RIFE interpolation Parent KFs → RIFE
R      Orange  Patch    RIFE + residual    RIFE → add patch
C      Purple  Stored   WebP decode        Direct (forced)
D      Red     N/A      Skipped            Error/skip
[/mono]

### Keyframe (K)
Full image stored as compressed WebP. Decoded directly. These are the "anchor" frames.

### Interpolated (I)
[color:cyan]NOT stored[/color]. Reconstructed by running RIFE on the two nearest parent keyframes. Uses GPU.

### Residual (R)
Reconstructed by RIFE, then a small [color:yellow]correction patch[/color] is added. Used when RIFE alone would lose face/body detail.

### Forced Keyframe (C)
Stored as full image, [color:accent]forced[/color] because:
• Scene cut detected
• Face quality would degrade
• Body motion too large
• Identity changed between frames

### Deleted (D)
Logically removed. Data still exists in archive until compacted.

