# Archive Format (.iarc) {#archive_format}

## File Structure
[mono]
┌─────────────────────────────────┐
│ MAGIC "IARC" (4 bytes)          │
│ VERSION (4 bytes, uint32)       │
│ HEADER_JSON_SIZE (8 bytes)      │
│ INDEX_JSON_SIZE (8 bytes)       │
├─────────────────────────────────┤
│ HEADER JSON (variable)          │
│   total_frames, codec, quality  │
│   dimensions, thresholds, etc.  │
├─────────────────────────────────┤
│ INDEX JSON (array of frames)    │
│   index, name, type, offsets    │
│   parents, timestep, scores     │
├─────────────────────────────────┤
│ DATA BLOCKS (sequential)        │
│   WebP keyframe blobs           │
│   WebP residual blobs           │
├─────────────────────────────────┤
│ FOOTER CHECKSUM (64 bytes)      │
│   SHA256 of everything above    │
└─────────────────────────────────┘
[/mono]

## Random Access
To read frame N:
1. Parse index from header
2. Look up frame N's offset and size
3. Seek directly to data offset
4. Read and decode

No need to read the entire file.

## Reconstruction Algorithm
[mono]
If KEYFRAME:     seek → read → decode WebP
If INTERPOLATED: get parent A + B → RIFE(A, B, timestep)
If RESIDUAL:     RIFE(A, B, t) → add stored residual patch
If DELETED:      skip / error
[/mono]

