# Troubleshooting {#troubleshooting}

## RIFE model fails to load
[color:yellow]Check:[/color]
• RIFE model directory path is correct in Settings
• Directory contains model files (flownet.pkl or similar)
• Use [b]Test RIFE[/b] button in Settings tab

## All frames shown as keyframes
[color:yellow]Check:[/color]
• Similarity threshold — try lowering to 0.85
• GOP size — try increasing to 16 or 24
• Ensure source images are actually sequential and similar

## Analysis takes too long
The fast analyzer should process 45k frames in 4-6 minutes.
If it takes longer:
• Disable Optical Flow (RAFT) — saves significant time
• Disable Identity Check — reduces AI phase
• Ensure GPU is being used (check GPU status indicator)

## FP16 type mismatch error
[color:red]RuntimeError: Input type Half and bias type float[/color]
The RIFE model must be fully converted to FP16. This is handled automatically. If you see this error:
• Go to Settings → GPU Precision → select FP32
• Or update to the latest RIFE model files

## CPU at 100% during analysis
• ONNX sessions may be using CPU — check Settings for CUDA device
• Reduce ONNX thread count in Settings
• Ensure onnxruntime-gpu is installed (not onnxruntime)

## Archive won't open
[color:yellow]Check:[/color]
• File is not corrupted — try Verify
• File has .iarc extension
• File starts with "IARC" magic bytes
• Try Repair if verification fails

## Video export fails
• Ensure ffmpeg is in your system PATH
• Try: [b]ffmpeg -version[/b] in command prompt
• Check output path is writable
• Ensure archive is open and has frames

## Tooltips appearing randomly
This was a known issue that has been fixed. If tooltips still misbehave:
• Only one tooltip should ever appear at a time
• Tooltips auto-hide after 8 seconds
• Moving the mouse hides the current tooltip

